zfp -- vendored into SZ3
========================

Upstream:  https://github.com/LLNL/zfp, release 0.3.1 (the C++ template headers
           from inc/)
License:   BSD-3-Clause (see the LICENSE file in this directory)

The files in this directory have been MODIFIED from the upstream sources listed
above, to modularize the codec for use as an SZ3 pipeline stage
(`ZFPDecomposition`, `ZFPEncoder`). BSD-3-Clause imposes no modification-notice
requirement; this file is provided so that maintainers upgrading the bundled
copy know what was changed and why.

Vendored files (14), all from upstream `inc/`:

    bitstream.h     fixedpoint32.h  fixedpoint64.h  intcodec.h
    intcodec04.h    intcodec16.h    intcodec64.h    intrinsics.h
    types.h         zfpcodec.h      zfpcodec1.h     zfpcodec2.h
    zfpcodec3.h     zfptransform.h

Modifications made by the SZ3 project:

1. Namespace change (all 14 files). `namespace ZFP` re-wrapped as
   `namespace SZ3::ZFP`, so that SZ3 can be linked alongside an independent
   build of upstream zfp without symbol collisions.

2. Access control (`zfpcodec1.h`, `zfpcodec2.h`, `zfpcodec3.h`). The `protected:`
   section of each codec class was changed to `public:`, so that SZ3's
   decomposition and encoder modules can drive the codec internals directly
   rather than through upstream's single-shot compression entry points. This is
   the change that makes the codec usable as a composable pipeline stage.

3. Portability (`intrinsics.h`). The fallback `lrint` guard was narrowed from
   `#ifndef HAVE_C99_MATH` to
   `#if defined(_MSC_VER) && _MSC_VER < 1800 && !defined(HAVE_C99_MATH)`, so the
   fallback applies only to pre-VS2013 MSVC and does not shadow the standard
   library on other toolchains.

4. Modernization (`bitstream.h`). `MemoryBitStream`'s member initializers use
   `nullptr` instead of `0`, and one C-style cast was replaced with
   `static_cast<uchar*>`.

5. Commented-out debug lines added (`intcodec04.h`, `intcodec64.h`,
   `zfpcodec3.h`). Three inactive `// printf(...)` diagnostics. These have no
   effect; they do not appear upstream.

6. Formatting (`zfpcodec1.h`). `precision()` reflowed across three lines.

`intcodec.h`, `intcodec16.h`, and `types.h` differ from upstream only by the
namespace wrap of item 1.

Upstream files carry no per-file copyright notices of their own, so none were
removed.

Citation: P. Lindstrom, "Fixed-Rate Compressed Floating-Point Arrays," IEEE
TVCG 20(12), 2014.
